Fabric Project 1 - Metadata Driven Incremental ETL Framework
1. Project Overview
Objective
Build a reusable Microsoft Fabric Pipeline capable of:
•	Reading metadata from a configuration table.
•	Processing multiple source tables automatically.
•	Performing Incremental Loads using Watermarks.
•	Performing Full Loads when incremental loading is unavailable.
•	Dynamically determining:
o	Source Table
o	Target Table
o	Watermark Column
o	Loading Strategy
The pipeline is metadata-driven, meaning that adding a new table requires only metadata insertion, not pipeline modification.
________________________________________
2. Business Problem
Suppose a company has many source tables:
Customers
Orders
Products
OrderDetails
Territories
The company wants:
•	One Pipeline.
•	One reusable framework.
•	Incremental loading where possible.
•	Full refresh for tables without watermarks.
•	No hardcoded table names.
________________________________________
3. Architecture
ConfigTable
      │
      ▼
MainLookup
      │
      ▼
ForEach (Sequential)
      │
      ▼
InnerLookup (Watermark)
      │
      ▼
If Condition

TRUE Branch
    Incremental Copy
    ↓
    Update Watermark

FALSE Branch
    Delete Target
    ↓
    Full Copy
________________________________________
4. Metadata Tables
ConfigTable
Stores metadata for each source.
Column	Description
SourceTable	Source table name
TargetTable	Destination table
WatermarkColumn	Incremental column
IsIncremental	True / False
IsActive	Active flag
Example:
SourceTable	TargetTable	WatermarkColumn	IsIncremental	IsActive
Customers	Customers_Target	ModifiedDate	True	True
Orders	Orders_Target	ModifiedDate	True	True
Products	Products_Target	ModifiedDate	False	True
OrderDetails	OrderDetails_Target	ModifiedDate	True	True
Territories	Territories_Target	ModifiedDate	True	True
________________________________________
WatermarkTable
Stores the last processed timestamp.
TableName	LastExecDate
Customers	2026-06-15
Orders	2026-06-10
Products	1900-01-01
OrderDetails	2026-06-12
Territories	2026-06-08
________________________________________
5. Main Lookup
Query:
SELECT *
FROM ConfigTable
WHERE IsActive = 1
Returns:
[
 {
   "SourceTable":"Customers",
   "TargetTable":"Customers_Target",
   "WatermarkColumn":"ModifiedDate",
   "IsIncremental":true
 }
]
________________________________________
6. ForEach
Items:
@activity('MainLookup').output.value
Purpose:
Loop through every active table automatically.
________________________________________
7. Inner Lookup
Purpose:
Retrieve the watermark for the current table.
Dynamic query:
@concat(
'SELECT LastExecDate
FROM WatermarkTable
WHERE TableName = ''',
item().SourceTable,
''''
)
Example:
Iteration:
Customers
Generated query:
SELECT LastExecDate
FROM WatermarkTable
WHERE TableName = 'Customers'
Output:
{
  "firstRow":
  {
     "LastExecDate":"2026-06-01T00:00:00Z"
  }
}
________________________________________
8. If Condition
Expression:
@equals(item().IsIncremental,true)
If:
True
go to:
Incremental Branch
If:
False
go to:
Full Load Branch
________________________________________
9. TRUE Branch - Incremental Load
Source Query:
@concat(
'SELECT * FROM ',
item().SourceTable,
' WHERE ModifiedDate > ''',
activity('InnerLookup').output.firstRow.LastExecDate,
''''
)
Generated:
SELECT *
FROM Customers
WHERE ModifiedDate > '2026-06-01'
________________________________________
Destination:
Schema:
dbo
Table:
@item().TargetTable
Example:
Customers_Target
________________________________________
10. Watermark Update
After successful copy:
Script:
@concat(
'UPDATE WatermarkTable
SET LastExecDate =
(
SELECT MAX(ModifiedDate)
FROM ',
item().SourceTable,
')
WHERE TableName = ''',
item().SourceTable,
''''
)
Generated:
UPDATE WatermarkTable
SET LastExecDate =
(
    SELECT MAX(ModifiedDate)
    FROM Customers
)
WHERE TableName='Customers'
________________________________________
11. FALSE Branch - Full Refresh
Some tables do not have:
•	ModifiedDate
•	LastUpdated
•	CDC columns
For these:
First:
Delete Target
Script:
@concat(
'DELETE FROM ',
item().TargetTable
)
Generated:
DELETE FROM Products_Target
________________________________________
Then:
Copy everything.
Source:
@concat(
'SELECT * FROM ',
item().SourceTable
)
Generated:
SELECT *
FROM Products
________________________________________
12. Duplicate Prevention Logic
Incremental Tables
Duplicates are prevented by:
WHERE ModifiedDate > LastExecDate
plus:
UPDATE WatermarkTable
after each successful load.
________________________________________
Full Load Tables
Duplicates are prevented by:
DELETE FROM TargetTable
before copying.
________________________________________
13. Concurrency Issue Encountered
Issue:
Snapshot isolation transaction aborted due to update conflict
Cause:
Multiple iterations updating:
WatermarkTable
simultaneously.
Solution:
ForEach
Sequential = True
This guarantees:
Customers
    ↓
Update Watermark

Orders
    ↓
Update Watermark

OrderDetails
    ↓
Update Watermark
one at a time.
